  "question": "Can one DuckDB plan validate, diagnose and digest a streamed typed population with canonical bytes, and what do its JSON, streaming and PostgreSQL-extension contracts allow?",
  "answers": [
    "I02",
    "I05",
    "I06",
    "I07"
  ],
  "method": "Run a fused plan over a nested token stream with four invariants, typed diagnostics and a per-block digest, and compare digests with the repository canonical JSON. Compare to_json and json_normalize output with canonical bytes case by case. Read malformed JSON with an explicit schema. Observe reader streaming, single use and plan shapes. Attach corpus_structure_dev read-only through the postgres extension and observe pushed queries and type mapping.",
